        "text_PiX6Xe": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "color_scheme": "scheme-10",
            "title": "OUR STORY",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "enable_highlight_text_color": false,
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "heading_color": "",
            "subheading": "",
            "text": "<p>Veloura began in 2016 at a kitchen table, where our founder — a jeweller's granddaughter — started stringing Japanese Miyuki beads one tiny glass cylinder at a time. She named the atelier after her grandmother Veloura, the woman who taught her that the pieces we wear become part of our story.</p><p>Today, a small team of artisans handcrafts every Veloura piece in our workshop: bead bracelets strung one bead at a time, gold vermeil over recycled sterling silver, freshwater pearls matched by hand for lustre. Nothing is mass-produced. Every piece is finished, checked, and wrapped by hand.</p>",
            "alignment": "center",
            "align_text": "left",
            "padding_left": 20,
            "padding_right": 20,
            "align_content_container": "none",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "btn--primary",
            "width": "50%",
            "mobile_color_scheme": "",
            "mobile_padding_left": 15,
            "mobile_padding_right": 15,
            "block_custom_class": "",
            "animations": "inherit"
          }
        }
